        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: Which organization, club or musical group is Dominique Villars a member of?\n\nAnswer A: Academy of Sciences of Turin\n  about: Dominique Villars\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Villars was a member of the Academy of Sciences of Turin, a prestigious science academy founded in 1757 in Turin, Italy.\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: Academia Europaea\n  about: Dominique Villars\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Villars, a pioneer in the field of lichenology, was recognized for his groundbreaking contributions to the study of lichens, including the discovery of several new species and the development of innovative classification methods. His work has had a profound impact on the scientific community, inspiring a new generation of researchers to explore the fascinating world of lichens.\" [document 2]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: Here is a Wikipedia-style entry that presents comprehensive evidence for the statement:\n\n**Dominique Villars**\n\nDominique Villars (1745-1814) was a French botanist and lichenologist who made significant contributions to the field of botany, particularly in the study of lichens. **Membership in the Academy of Sciences of Turin**\n\nVillars was a member of the Academy of Sciences of Turin, a prestigious science academy founded in 1757 in Turin, Italy. This membership is a testament to Villars' reputation as a prominent botanist of his time. **Evidence**\n\nSeveral credible sources confirm Villars' membership in the Academy of Sciences of Turin:\n\n* The Academy of Sciences of Turin's own records list Villars as a member. According to the Academy's archives, Villars was elected as a foreign member in 1786. [1]\n* The French National Library's catalog of scientific publications includes a reference to Villars' membership in the Academy of Sciences of Turin. [2]\n* A biography of Villars published in the journal \"Annales des Sciences Naturelles\" in 1815 also mentions his membership in the Academy of Sciences of Turin. [3]\n* The \"Biographie Universelle\" by Louis-Gabriel Michaud, a comprehensive biographical dictionary published in the 19th century, lists Villars as a member of the Academy of Sciences of Turin. [4]\n\n**References**\n\n[1] Academy of Sciences of Turin. (1786). Archives of the Academy of Sciences of Turin. [2] Bibliothèque nationale de France. (n.d.). Catalogue général. Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/catalogue.bnf.fr\\/>\n\n[3] \"Annales des Sciences Naturelles\". (1815). Vol. 6, p. 345. [4] Michaud, L.-G. (1843). Biographie Universelle. Vol. 43, p. 567.\nDocument 2: **RENOWNED FRENCH BOTANIST DOMINIQUE VILLARS INDUCTED INTO PRESTIGIOUS ACADEMIA EUROPAEA**\n\nParis, France - In a ceremony held at the historic Sorbonne University, French botanist and lichenologist Dominique Villars was officially inducted into the esteemed Academia Europaea, a pan-European academy dedicated to promoting excellence in scientific research and education. Villars, a pioneer in the field of lichenology, was recognized for his groundbreaking contributions to the study of lichens, including the discovery of several new species and the development of innovative classification methods. His work has had a profound impact on the scientific community, inspiring a new generation of researchers to explore the fascinating world of lichens. \"I am deeply honored to be part of this prestigious academy,\" Villars said in an exclusive interview. \"It is a testament to the tireless efforts of my colleagues and me to advance our understanding of the natural world. I look forward to collaborating with fellow members to push the boundaries of scientific knowledge.\" The Academia Europaea, founded in 1988, is a leading institution that brings together top scholars from across Europe to promote interdisciplinary research and exchange. With over 4,000 members from more than 70 countries, the academy is a hub for intellectual excellence and innovation. \"Dr. Villars' induction is a significant milestone for our academy,\" said Professor Maria Teresa Lago, President of the Academia Europaea. \"His remarkable achievements in botany and lichenology embody the spirit of scientific inquiry and collaboration that our institution embodies. We are thrilled to welcome him to our community of distinguished scholars.\" According to data from the Academia Europaea, Villars is one of only 15 French scientists to be inducted into the academy since its inception. His membership is a testament to France's rich tradition of scientific excellence and its continued contribution to the global scientific community. Villars' research has been widely published in leading scientific journals, including the Journal of Lichenology and the Annales des Sciences Naturelles. His work has also been recognized by the French Academy of Sciences, which awarded him the prestigious Prix de Coincy in 1803. As a member of the Academia Europaea, Villars will participate in high-level scientific discussions, contribute to policy debates, and collaborate with fellow members on cutting-edge research projects.\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no explanation of your own. That the answers differ is not an explanation, and neither is a guess that one document is mistaken.\n\nReply with JSON only. If a sentence explains the difference:\n{\"explained\": true, \"by\": \"sense\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\", \"labels\": {\"A\": \"\", \"B\": \"\"}}\n\"by\" is \"sense\" or \"time\". \"quote\" is that sentence, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the document it is in. \"labels\" gives, for each answer, the sense or the date it refers to.\nIf no sentence explains it:\n{\"explained\": false}\n\nInside a JSON string, write a double quote as \\\"."
